### 2. Control Plane vs Data Plane

| Component | Control Plane (Databricks-managed) | Data Plane (Your Cloud Account) |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **What lives here** | Web UI, REST APIs, Notebooks, Job configs, Unity Catalog metadata | Compute (clusters/warehouses), Data files, DBFS |
| **Who manages** | Databricks | You (your Azure/AWS/GCP subscription) |
| **Network** | Databricks cloud account | Your VNet/VPC |
| **Key implication** | Metadata never leaves Databricks | Data never leaves your cloud account |
| **Exam tip** | Credentials are stored in the control plane (encrypted) | Results and data are processed in the data plane |

### 3. Workspace Hierarchy

```
Databricks Account
 ├── Workspace 1 (Dev)
 │    ├── Users / Groups / Service Principals
 │    ├── Notebooks, Repos, Files
 │    ├── Jobs, Pipelines
 │    └── Compute (Clusters, Warehouses)
 ├── Workspace 2 (Prod)
 └── Unity Catalog Metastore (shared across workspaces)
      ├── Catalog 1
      │    ├── Schema A
      │    │    ├── Tables, Views, Volumes, Functions
      │    │    └── Models (ML)
      │    └── Schema B
      └── Catalog 2
```

### 4. Key Services at a Glance

| Service | What It Does | Exam Weight | Key Commands |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **Delta Lake** | ACID storage layer on Parquet + transaction log | HIGH | `DESCRIBE DETAIL`, `DESCRIBE HISTORY`, `OPTIMIZE`, `VACUUM`, `RESTORE` |
| **Unity Catalog** | Centralized governance: access, lineage, sharing | HIGH | `GRANT`, `REVOKE`, `SHOW GRANTS`, `CREATE CATALOG/SCHEMA` |
| **Lakeflow Jobs** | Orchestration: schedule notebooks, pipelines, SQL | HIGH | Job UI, REST API, task dependencies |
| **Spark Declarative Pipelines (SDP)** | Declarative ETL with quality expectations | MEDIUM | `CREATE STREAMING TABLE`, `CREATE MATERIALIZED VIEW`, expectations |
| **Databricks SQL** | SQL analytics with warehouses | HIGH | SQL Warehouse config, query profile, dashboards |
| **MLflow** | ML experiment tracking, model registry, serving | MEDIUM | `mlflow.log_param`, `mlflow.log_metric`, model stages |
| **Auto Loader** | Incremental file ingestion (cloud_files) | HIGH | `cloud_files`, `cloudFiles.format`, schema inference/evolution |
| **Repos / Git** | Version control integration | LOW | Git integration, CI/CD |
| **Secrets** | Credential management | LOW | `dbutils.secrets.get()`, secret scopes |
| **Delta Sharing** | Cross-org data sharing (open protocol) | MEDIUM | `CREATE SHARE`, `CREATE RECIPIENT`, `GRANT SELECT ON SHARE` |
